at will and reincedinto a Gnome-ranger; that is a gnome fighter with the ranger ability to tameanimals. I thought that the animal would do the tanking and fighting for mebut in the end it turned out to be quite useless.So I gained some exp. with taming wolves and letting them fight (and kill themafter they'd done their job and ran low on hp's). At some point I tried totame salamanders at well but that didn't work at all. (pity ;)Anyway things weren't going like I wanted so I reinced into something else andthen the message came up that I still had an animal walking around somewhere.Well actually I'm quite sure that either I killed the last animal I'd tamed orit had been killed for me by some other monster. So I'm quite sure that I wasnot the master of any animal anymore but the game consisted I was.Since ranger-subguild seemed to have lost its interest for me I wasn't trainingany animal taming levels anymore and just continued playing after the reinc.At the end of the day I tried to safe_quit which didn't work, even quit didn'twork and I got myself killed hoping that would clear up stuff which still didnot work ;(Coming back the following day I noticed that the mud-clock hadn't moved on andsomewhat after I got your e-mail. Well hope this is sufficient information toyou. Happy hunting!Drude**Gynter**Subj: need some helpDate: May  8Hola :)I am on lastlastlast touch of my areases... (2in1 kinda deal)But I have a problem.. I have two guards guarding the king in onearea and they should attack when the king is attacked.(preferably make the attacker hit them instead)But I cannot make them attack... The only thing they do isShout the line I make them shout (this shows nothing wrong with catch_tell)If you could take a look at it I would be veryveryvery happy :)(I asked onarion and celtron but they have _ALOTTA_ work apparentlyso I thought is better to ask you)The files of the guard and king is in /wizards/gynter/area2/city1/mobsand 