uliskilttikungkku.Razinduktha on rival thanen chief, ja on vallannu castle northfacen, ja upkeeppaa siella sen iiwoldwarffeja, jotka tappaa kaikki, koska ne on xenophobicmission: 1) free warlock + tappoa2) free irthun + kuuntele mita se sanoo3) tapa razindukhta, joka ei tykkaa YHTAAN siita mita sa teet4) loyda, ja mercifully slay khilari, loottaa crowni ja palauta se irthunilleniin se proclaimaa ittensa kingiks5) irthun on ihan basic monsu, eika sita kannata tappaa expasta tai ees ekusta,mut ku khilari on tapettu, ni paikka on 'freed of the dark powers', ja ne dwarffitjotka \"periaatteessa\" on survivennu, alkaa worshippaa irthunia, ja se tajuu ettei setarvii crownia, rullatakseen naamojairthuni istuu jossain upupupissa ja sit ku menee sinne, ni se kertoo tarinan, miten loytaa molempiin monsuihinsitten irthun sanoo et \"thanks man for setting me free, ma lahen nyt seikkailee, ja yritan raisee resistancee\"(tietty se on niin pelle ettei se saa mitaan oikeesti aikaseks)OKOO!! nyt siis tiedetaan missa se iiwol warlock on, vaikka seonki cagessa, ni sen dark aura on cause tahan kaikkeenja tiedetaan minne se undiid khilarbhunaz on lukittu.Mennaan tappaa jannut, ja silta khilarilta saa sellasen cloakin missa on sen dwarven kingdomin oikee symbolKeskella courtyardia (as it so happens) sattuu olee lipputanko, missa on sen Razindukthan (eli se joka on raidannuja ilkeilee siella linnassa) symboli salossa. Se lippu pitaa ottaa alas, ja \"cut cloak\" niin etta sinne jaa reika, ja sitten hissata se toinen symbol sinne salkoon, jolloin tiedetaan etta se linna on \"liberated\"...Out of nowhere (WHOA!!!!) appearaa se irthun joka alkaa thankyouthankyouthankyou(moby style) sua, ja sanoo et jumalauta oot kova jannu ku teit tan tempun. Annetaan crown sille irthunille ja se sanoo thankyouthankyouthankyouthankyou. Sitten taas (OUT OF NOWHERE) appearaa joku (tshybys tms) ja sanoo sille etta 'you need not that crown to rule this place, you are bound to it by blood) (ainii, ala kysy miten se on saannu pojanpojanpojanpoikia). No, se on vahan silleen what the perkele is going on, ja lahtee vittuun siita sikalasta sen eukon kanssa. MUTTA... Now comes the jännä kohta.Se irthuni onki yhtakkia teleportannu sen arean exitille, ja se on siella heilumassa sen crownin kanssa.sit se selittaa etta \"joojoo, toi tshybys ei anna pimperoo ennenku ma luovun tasta crownista\", ni se antaa sen sulleja se onki ihan suffeli eku. sit se cloak jossa on big hole in the middle on kans jotain kovaa, ja muilta monsuilta saa kans jannia juttujama osaan ihan hyvin ton basic coden, mut noissa KIKKAILU kohdissa on sellasia mita sun/meijan pitaa teha...katellaanpop**Walla**Subj: vahan selvennystaCc: wallaDate: Mar  3joo, eli meni jotain nimia sekasin, ku keksin niita sitamukaan mita kirjotineli: Irthun on sellanen kiltti jannu, se joka helppaileeRazindukhta on se enemy clanista tullu jannu joka teki his dirty works ja rules the place with an iron grip ja oppressaa kaikkiaKhazin-Talak on dwarven deathknight, joo, eika warlock (dwarven deathknight ois kyl varmaan hauska oikeesti naha) sellanen pikku jannu joka vetaa sua pataan 100-0, no mut...Khilarbhunaz on se old king, joka oli siella minding his business ku se Khazin-Talak tuli sinne riehumaan(history excerpt: the siege of castle northface...khazin-talak ja Razindukhtan isoisoisoisoisä Razag-Garan ja niitten army tuli sinne northfaceen vetaa niita lattyn, koskathey had nothing better to do on a sunday afternoon tms.During the battle, Razindukhta got severly wounded perhaps even mortally, joo mortally wounded... HAHAA yllattava kaanne tulee tassa vaiheessa!Eli se khazin-Talak, ei oikeesti ollu iiwol siina vaiheessa viela, mut sit ku se woundaantu se kunkku, ni se meni sinnepatemaan etta joojoo ma hinaan sut ja pannaan sut iskuun, ja tapetaan se helvetin razag-garan pelle, ja heitetaan se vittuun tasta sikalastataa on meijan mesta, ja me ollaan bestest.sit se drawwas daggerin, ja veti throatin auki, ja castas jonku spellin et se pysty tekee siita undeadin.MUTTA!Kabun-Nural, joka oli Razindukhtan poika, ehti heittaa sen Khazin-Talakin jonnekki vitun kuuseen sinne castlen basementtiinmagically sealed hakkiinjossa sita deathknightia on ottanu paahan viimeset 3000 vuotta tmsNo, vaikka se Razindukhta on nyt undead, ja todella EVIL ja se tappaa kaikki mita liikkuu, ni se ei pystyny tappaa omaa poikaansakoska jotain bloodbond tms, tai sit se poika jotenki vaan dodges sen stabit jnemutta, se poika sit captures sen faijan, ja pani sen lukkojen taakse ihan vaan for the protection of the world.No, eihan se ikina kertonu juurikaan kenelle etta miten sen saa pois sielta, koska se fearas etta maailma menee rikki jos sen freeaa.Nyt tassa vaiheessa historiassa on jotain pienia glitcheja mut kuitenkitoitoitoi, oota scrollaanvittu, oon nyt puhunu razindukhtasta kingina, ku se oli oikeesti se ilkee jannunii, eli khilarbhunaz oli se kiltti kingi jota betrayattiin, ja stabbattiin, ja josta tehtiin undead jnenoni, eli siis tassa vaiheessa sen razindukhtan isoisoisoisa Razag-Garan stormaa sen castlen, koska niilla oli jotain helppereitajotka jeesas, eli lisaa traitoreita, mita se khazin-talak (joo se elaa edelleen, koska se on deathknight(undead)jaa, sulku kiinni)oli convertannu jotain niista kilteista dwarffeista sellasiks iivoleiksnoni, ja ne sit tietenki slayas sen khilarbhunaksen pojan, ennen ku se ehti sanoo miten se liberatetaan(tai sit se teki suiciden, ja vei secretin tombiin...)sillaki oli jo poika tulossa, mut jossain safe placessa, se oli paassy selkaan sellasen karvasen dwarfmuijan kanssanoni, no nyt many years later, ni se Irthun sneakkas sinne linnaan, ja alko ettimaan kaikkia juttuja, ja se loys secretkirjan, jossa kerrotaan taa tarina, seoli joku Dwarven chronicler mita ei oo enaa olemassa, joka oli kirjottanu sen kirjanja se sit loys naa jutut, varmaanki sen takia koska sen ancestorin spirit leadas sita oikeeseen paikkaanno, nyt aletaan jo paasee to the pointJoku sit loys sen sielta hiippailemasta, mut se ehti tuhoo sen kirjan, joten se on nyt ainoo maailmassa (whole wide world) joka tietaa miten sen saa freeattua...Tietty taa Razindukhta, joka oli se iivil grandson haluu liberateta sen dk:n ja sen spiritin, ja cast the world upon a dark age tmsnoni, nyt se on jossain tornissa, ja sita torturetaan, koska ne haluu tietaa miten sinne paaseeJa pointtina on tietenkin taas pelastaa maailma jne jne jnehistory excerpt ends here tms)hoovee, nyt oon selitelly ihan liikaa, teen sellasen bookin jonnekki torchholderin taakse, ni muutki voi lukee mun sekoilujaemma tiia jos taa autto yhtaan, varmaan vaan sekottimut \"i'll get my shit together\" ja kirjotan ton puhtaaks, hyva tarina seon, vaikkakin ihan adlibbattu tassa ku kirjottelen, pitaaki CC:walla et saan sen itenoni, joosoittele tai telli tai jotain... flamee vaikka-pop**Walla**Subj: the siege of northfaceDate: Mar  3The Siege of Castle Northface,As recorded by the dwarven Chronicler Nural-Girulin the year 581 of the dwarven calendar.(start of excerpt...)Khilarbhunaz's long reign of prosperity has led the dwarves of Northface tobecome wealthy, and well known over the continent as good merchants of steeland other metals. Khilarbhunaz' son and heir, Kabun-Nural, is 10 years awayfrom becoming the new Thane. But in the south, a shadow looms.Khilarbhunaz's good friend and advisor, the powerful death knight Khazin-Talakhas warned the Thane for many years now of a rivalling clan, lead by theaggressive Razag-Garan, and of his anger towards the friendly Northern dwarves.In the fall, after the harvest of the season had been recovered, messenger wassent by Khilarbhunaz to Razag-Garan to find out the reason for the hostilespeakings of his cousin. After a month of waiting, another messenger was sentout, as the first one never returned. Another month passed by, and Khilarbhunazstarted to get worried. He sent out a group of soldiers to accompagny a thirdmessenger. Three weeks later one dwarf returned to the Castle, clothes torn,and long gashes of blood running down his face. An arm had been chopped off,aswell as one of his legs. His beard had been ripped off, and he was deliriousfrom the lack of water.The returning dwarven soldier, Unazdalgur, told of what he had seen, andKhilarbhunaz and his counsil turned pale as death itself. The two first messengerswere found hanging from their beards from the castle South Keep, with their stomachsgutted out, and spilled on the ground. All limbs had been hacked off and were placedbelow the poor messengers. The same thing had been done to the third messengeraswell as the military escort. Unazdalgur said that he was lucky to have left the placealive, but thought that there was a clear reason why he had not been slain, but toreport the truth. Razag-Garan was to attack in the near future, and a complete destructionof the northern dwarves seemed imminent. Khilarbhunaz quickly sent the women and children away, to a remote location, still unknownto the rest of the world, via tunnels from castle Northface. The tunnels were then sealed offfor eternity. Despite the reluctance of the thane, Khilarbhunaz's son, Kabun-Nural stayed at thecastle, only sending away his wife Karalgunda and their unborn child.Two days after, the largest demonstration of power on the continent up to then was displayedas Razag-Garan's troops besieged castle Northface. A griffon that happened to fly over the castlein those dire days could see that the grounds around the castle was blackened by dwarves in a 10 mile radius.Huge encampments were set up in front of the castle, and eventhough Khilarbhunaz tried many timesto send messengers to confere with Razag-Garan they all returned having not even seen a man in chargeor slain instantly.For the whole autumn, and beginning of winter, Khilarbhunaz and his dwarves were starved out in theircastle, with nothing to do. On the day of the winter solstice, during the evening, Razag-Garan's troops opened fire on the castle. During this assault, Khilarbhunaz was severly injured, and taken to his quarters, where only few of his closest advisors were permitted.Khilarbhunaz summoned for his friend Khazin-Talak, for he could surely cure him, although his dedicationto the darker side of the arts of magic. On the darkest moment of the year, at midnight Khazin-Talak drewa dagger from his sleeve, and slit Khilarbhunaz's throat, while chanting dark incantations of magic.Khazin-Talak drew blood and removed Khilarbhunaz's heart, and fed it to the dying dwarven king, in hopeof ressurecting him as a lich, and succeeded.A small group of soldiers, loyal to Khazin-Talak then started killing the dwarves within the castle. A fearce battle started, and Khazin-Talak along with his lich slew many themselves. Kabun-Nural succeeded in locking the deathknight into a magically sealed cage, and hid it somewhere deep within the mountains heart. Khilarbhunaz, however enraged at the capturing of his master could not bring himself to kill his own son, and was defeated. Kabun-Nural locked the lich into a magically guarded tower, from where he could no longer harm anyone. But the battle was far from over. A group of soldiers, loyal to Khazin-Talakhad secretly opened the huge gates to the castle, and Razag-Garan's troops invaded the castle, slaying the rest of the resistance. Before Kabun-Nural was captured, he scribbled a book on destroying the creatures, hid it and leaped from the top of one of the towers into the mountains below, preventing anyone of finding out how to release the evil creations, spawned that night.But some things that should not have been forgotten, were lost...(end of excerpt...)Year 4016. dwarven calendar.(start of excerpt...)My Name is Irthun, and I am one of the decendants of Khilarbhunaz. I have just learned the true story of my ancestors, and I am appauled by the lack of respect that my ancestors cousin had for him. My people have long sang the song of Kanu, which I believe to be no other than Kabun-Nural's legacy of how to find and destroy once and for all the evil spirits that haunt the world and this castle. I have come here in search for a military training, but I fear that Razindukhta, the new Thane can see right through me, and will capture me if they can find me. I found the book that Kabun-Nural hid behind him in the castle, after 27 years of searching, and destroyed it. Now, I am the only one that knows the way to rid the world of the most dangerous threat it has ever known. If you find me, say the password and I will help you... Say her name to me thrice, and you will be helped. If I am found and tortured, I don't know how long I can hold out. If anyone happens to find this book, you will know that the old folk stories are all but stories, and you must destroy Khazin-Talak and Khilarbhunaz, aswell as Razindukhta and his followers. I have added some parchments of the text in destroying them here, but the ink has already started to fade badly, and I am afraid that further handling of them will prove disasterous.My light is running low, and I must soon find another refuge in the castle. Please find me, and help us all.-Irthun(end of excerpt...)**Devil**Subj: level wishDate: Mar  6mulla meni leba wishi rebirthissä!**Gynter**Subj: elemental areaDate: Mar  7I think this will suffice..Cords: 148 34Entryroom: /wizards/gynter/element/gateway.cQuests: Destroy the entrance to the fire plane			Destroy the pillar to the air realm			Destroy the gateway to the earth plane			Destroy the entrance to the water plane 		Release the great spirit element			Give vorpal blade to the lord of Air	Give pouch to the stone elemental	Return the key to the Fire Demon	Return the icecube to the great white sharkThere :)/gynt'man**Gynter**Subj: area...Date: Mar 10Ok some errors :) First I ga